{
  "verdict": "weak",
  "critique": "The strategy never generated a trade, indicating overly restrictive entry filters (ADX > 25 plus volume oscillator sign) on a 4h BCH/USDC chart, and a mismatch between the intended market (BCHUSDC) and the back‑test context (MOVEUSDC 3m). This prevents any assessment of signal quality, robustness, or over‑fitting. Risk controls (ATR stop/TP) are described but not exercised, and there are no tests for parameter sensitivity, walk‑forward stability, or Monte‑Carlo drawdown. Consequently the current build offers no actionable insight and cannot be trusted for production.",
  "next_focus": [
    "Align back‑test symbol and timeframe with the objective (use BCHUSDC 4h).",
    "Relax entry thresholds (e.g., lower ADX threshold, add a minimum volume filter) to achieve a minimum trade count for statistical relevance.",
    "Implement and verify the ATR‑based stop‑loss and take‑profit logic in the back‑test.",
    "Add robustness checks: parameter sweep, walk‑forward validation, and Monte‑Carlo simulations to expose over‑fitting."
  ]
}

